abstract: >
  This repository contains the code, data, and model checkpoints for the paper
  "Residue-Level Attributions in Protein Language Models Do Not Recover Allergen
  Epitopes", accepted at the ICML 2026 Workshop on Mechanistic Interpretability.
  The paper benchmarks whether residue-level attribution scores (Integrated Gradients,
  Gradient x Input, SmoothGrad) from protein language models align with
  experimentally annotated allergen epitopes from the IEDB database.

keywords:
  - protein language models
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - allergenicity
  - integrated gradients
  - attribution methods
  - ESM-2
  - IEDB
  - epitope localization
  - bioinformatics

